---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Notice — BP Analyst"
  description="Draft cookie notice for the BP Analyst marketing site. For qualified counsel review."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="legal__header">
      <p class="legal__eyebrow">Legal draft</p>
      <h1 class="legal__title">Cookie Notice</h1>
      <p class="legal__lede">
        <strong>Draft for qualified legal counsel review.</strong> Applies to
        the marketing website only. Last updated 6 November 2026.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal__body">
      <section>
        <h2>What we use</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> a local consent preference in{' '}
          <code>localStorage</code> (<code>bp-analyst-analytics-consent</code>)
          so we can remember Accept or Reject. The site works without analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Analytics (optional):</strong> Google Analytics 4 and/or
          Yandex Metrika, only if measurement IDs are configured. The Google tag
          may load under Consent Mode with analytics storage denied until you
          Accept; Yandex Metrika loads only after Accept. After Accept, vendors
          may set cookies or similar identifiers and process IP, device, and
          usage data. Reject keeps analytics storage off.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How to choose</h2>
        <p>
          On first visit (when analytics IDs are configured) a banner offers
          Accept analytics or Reject with equal prominence. Change your mind
          anytime via{' '}
          <a href="#consent" data-open-consent>
            Cookie settings
          </a>{' '}
          in the footer. Clearing site data resets the choice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Extension</h2>
        <p>
          The browser extension does not embed these marketing analytics SDKs.
          It uses browser extension storage for local analysis only — see{' '}
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>More detail</h2>
        <p>
          Recipients, retention, and transfer mechanisms are summarized in the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> draft and should be finalized
          with counsel before treating this notice as final.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .legal {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: calc(5.5rem + var(--space-7)) var(--space-9);
      max-inline-size: 42rem;
    }

    .legal__eyebrow {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-fg-subtle);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .legal__title {
      margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .legal__lede {
      margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
      color: var(--color-fg-muted);
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .legal__body {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-7);
    }

    .legal__body h2 {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .legal__body p {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
      color: var(--color-fg-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .legal__body p:last-child {
      margin-block-end: 0;
    }

    .legal__body a {
      color: var(--color-accent);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    }

    .legal__body code {
      font-size: 0.92em;
      color: var(--color-fg);
    }
  }
</style>
